{"name":"Cal Poly Pomona Green","hex":"#1e4d2b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["calorie","ISO 639-3 language code for Carolinian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of calorie.","Clipping of caliber."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cal"},{"term":"poly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A polytechnic.","Polyethylene (polythene)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Polyamorous."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poly"},{"term":"pomona","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A treatise on fruits."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pomona"}],"entries":[{"title":"California State Polytechnic University, Pomona","blocks":[{"text":"California State Polytechnic University, Pomona is a public polytechnic research university in Pomona, California, United States. Designated R2, Doctoral Universities – High Research Activity. It is the largest of the three polytechnic universities in the California State University system by enrollment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/California_Polytechnic_%28Pomona%29_university_seal.svg/330px-California_Polytechnic_%28Pomona%29_university_seal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_State_Polytechnic_University%2C_Pomona","wikidata":"Q1026868"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/CalPoly_Stables.jpg/500px-CalPoly_Stables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/CalPoly_Stables.jpg/1280px-CalPoly_Stables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/CalPoly_Stables.jpg/500px-CalPoly_Stables.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old horse stables","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalPoly_Stables.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/W.K._Kellogg_with_Antez_%281929%29.PNG/330px-W.K._Kellogg_with_Antez_%281929%29.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/W.K._Kellogg_with_Antez_%281929%29.PNG/330px-W.K._Kellogg_with_Antez_%281929%29.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cal Poly Pomona stands on the former Arabian horse ranch of cereal magnate W.K. Kellogg.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AW.K._Kellogg_with_Antez_(1929).PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.